  {
   "id": "logistic-z",
   "scene": "LogisticZSequence",
   "section": 1,
   "title": "The substitution $z = 1/y$ makes the logistic equation linear",
   "summary": "The chain rule, one division by $y^2$, a linear solve, and a flip back to $y$.",
   "initial": {
    "title": "Growth with competition",
    "tex": "y' = a\\,y - b\\,y^2",
    "explanation": "Births minus competition. The $y^2$ term makes it nonlinear.",
    "frame": "animations/logistic-z/state-00.jpg"
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "index": 1,
     "title": "Chain rule for $z = 1/y$",
     "relation": "define",
     "relationLabel": "Definition / choice",
     "tex": "z = \\frac{1}{y} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; z' = -\\frac{y'}{y^2}",
     "explanation": "The derivative of $y^{-1}$ is $-y^{-2}$, times $y'$.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/logistic-z/state-00.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/logistic-z/state-01.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/logistic-z/step-01.mp4",
      "duration": 3.1,
      "frames": 93,
      "masterFrames": [
       8,
       101
      ],
      "bytes": 41891,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 2,
     "title": "Substitute $y'$",
     "relation": "substitute",
     "relationLabel": "Substitution",
     "tex": "z' = -\\frac{a y - b y^2}{y^2} = -\\frac{a}{y} + b = -a z + b",
     "explanation": "Divide each term by $y^2$. What remains is $1/y = z$ to the first power: a linear equation.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/logistic-z/state-01.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/logistic-z/state-02.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/logistic-z/step-02.mp4",
      "duration": 4.5667,
      "frames": 137,
      "masterFrames": [
       100,
       237
      ],
      "bytes": 86038,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "title": "Solve, then flip",
     "relation": "solve",
     "relationLabel": "Solve",
     "tex": "z = \\frac{b}{a} + \\Big(z(0) - \\frac{b}{a}\\Big)e^{-at} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; y = \\frac{a}{b + d\\,e^{-at}}",
     "explanation": "Steady value $b/a$ plus a decaying null part. Then $y = 1/z$, with $d = a/y(0) - b$.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/logistic-z/state-02.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/logistic-z/state-03.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/logistic-z/step-03.mp4",
      "duration": 3.6333,
      "frames": 109,
      "masterFrames": [
       236,
       345
      ],
      "bytes": 146774,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    }
   ],
   "totalDuration": 11.3,
   "masterFrames": 345,
   "renderSeconds": 7.8
  },
  {
   "id": "s-curve",
   "scene": "SCurveSequence",
   "section": 1,
   "title": "S-curves between the steady states $0$ and $a/b$",
   "summary": "From $y(0) = 1/4$ the solution bends at half capacity; every positive start ends at $a/b$.",
   "initial": {
    "title": "Axes for $y' = y - y^2$",
    "tex": "y' = y - y^2 \\quad (a = b = 1)",
    "explanation": "Carrying capacity $a/b = 1$.",
    "frame": "animations/s-curve/state-00.jpg"
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "index": 1,
     "title": "One S-curve",
     "relation": "diagram",
     "relationLabel": "Picture",
     "tex": "y = \\frac{1}{1 + 3e^{-t}}",
     "explanation": "Starting at $1/4$: slow, fast, slow.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/s-curve/state-00.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/s-curve/state-01.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/s-curve/step-01.mp4",
      "duration": 2.5333,
      "frames": 76,
      "masterFrames": [
       8,
       84
      ],
      "bytes": 29070,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 2,
     "title": "The bend at half capacity",
     "relation": "compute",
     "relationLabel": "Computation",
     "tex": "y'' = (1 - 2y)\\,y' = 0 \\;\\text{ at } y = \\tfrac12,\\ t = \\ln 3",
     "explanation": "Growth is fastest where $y = a/(2b)$.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/s-curve/state-01.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/s-curve/state-02.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/s-curve/step-02.mp4",
      "duration": 3.1,
      "frames": 93,
      "masterFrames": [
       83,
       176
      ],
      "bytes": 46667,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "title": "Other starting values",
     "relation": "implies",
     "relationLabel": "Consequence (⇒)",
     "tex": "y(0) > 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; y(t) \\to \\frac{a}{b}",
     "explanation": "From below the curve rises, from above it falls; $0$ repels and $1$ attracts.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/s-curve/state-02.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/s-curve/state-03.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/s-curve/step-03.mp4",
      "duration": 3.5667,
      "frames": 107,
      "masterFrames": [
       175,
       282
      ],
      "bytes": 72548,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    }
   ],
   "totalDuration": 9.2,
   "masterFrames": 282,
   "renderSeconds": 7.4
  },
  {
   "id": "stability-test",
   "scene": "StabilityTestSequence",
   "section": 2,
   "title": "The slope $f'(Y)$ decides stability",
   "summary": "Tangent lines of $f(y) = y - y^2$ at its roots: slope $+1$ at $0$, $-1$ at $1$.",
   "initial": {
    "title": "Graph of $f$",
    "tex": "y' = f(y) = y - y^2",
    "explanation": "The height of the graph is the velocity of $y$.",
    "frame": "animations/stability-test/state-00.jpg"
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "index": 1,
     "title": "Steady states are roots",
     "relation": "solve",
     "relationLabel": "Solve",
     "tex": "f(Y) = Y(1 - Y) = 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; Y = 0,\\ Y = 1",
     "explanation": "Where the graph crosses zero, $y$ does not move.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/stability-test/state-00.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/stability-test/state-01.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/stability-test/step-01.mp4",
      "duration": 2.3,
      "frames": 69,
      "masterFrames": [
       8,
       77
      ],
      "bytes": 29175,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 2,
     "title": "Tangent lines at the roots",
     "relation": "compute",
     "relationLabel": "Computation",
     "tex": "f'(y) = 1 - 2y:\\quad f'(0) = +1,\\quad f'(1) = -1",
     "explanation": "Near each root, $f$ looks like its tangent line.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/stability-test/state-01.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/stability-test/state-02.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/stability-test/step-02.mp4",
      "duration": 2.7,
      "frames": 81,
      "masterFrames": [
       76,
       157
      ],
      "bytes": 51721,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "title": "The linear equation for the gap",
     "relation": "implies",
     "relationLabel": "Consequence (⇒)",
     "tex": "(y - Y)' \\approx f'(Y)\\,(y - Y) \\;\\Rightarrow\\; y - Y \\approx C\\,e^{f'(Y)t}",
     "explanation": "Negative slope: the gap decays (stable). Positive slope: it grows (unstable).",
     "initialFrame": "animations/stability-test/state-02.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/stability-test/state-03.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/stability-test/step-03.mp4",
      "duration": 3.2667,
      "frames": 98,
      "masterFrames": [
       156,
       254
      ],
      "bytes": 131235,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    }
   ],
   "totalDuration": 8.267,
   "masterFrames": 254,
   "renderSeconds": 7.6
