  {
   "id": "partial-fractions",
   "scene": "PartialFractionsSequence",
   "section": 3,
   "title": "The logistic equation by partial fractions",
   "summary": "Split $1/(y - y^2)$ into two simple fractions, integrate to logarithms, and solve.",
   "initial": {
    "title": "Separated logistic equation",
    "tex": "\\frac{dy}{y - y^2} = dt",
    "explanation": "Here $g(t) = 1$ and $f(y) = 1/(y - y^2)$.",
    "frame": "animations/partial-fractions/state-00.jpg"
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "index": 1,
     "title": "Factor and split",
     "relation": "identity",
     "relationLabel": "Identity (=)",
     "tex": "\\frac{1}{y(1 - y)} = \\frac{A}{y} + \\frac{B}{1 - y}",
     "explanation": "Two simple poles, at $y = 0$ and $y = 1$.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/partial-fractions/state-00.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/partial-fractions/state-01.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/partial-fractions/step-01.mp4",
      "duration": 2.5333,
      "frames": 76,
      "masterFrames": [
       8,
       84
      ],
      "bytes": 44815,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 2,
     "title": "Find $A$ and $B$",
     "relation": "compute",
     "relationLabel": "Computation",
     "tex": "1 = A(1 - y) + B\\,y \\;\\Rightarrow\\; A = 1 \\ (y = 0),\\ \\ B = 1 \\ (y = 1)",
     "explanation": "Multiply through by $y(1-y)$ and put in the two roots.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/partial-fractions/state-01.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/partial-fractions/state-02.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/partial-fractions/step-02.mp4",
      "duration": 3.1,
      "frames": 93,
      "masterFrames": [
       83,
       176
      ],
      "bytes": 120383,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 3,
     "title": "Integrate to logarithms",
     "relation": "compute",
     "relationLabel": "Computation",
     "tex": "\\ln|y| - \\ln|1 - y| = t + C",
     "explanation": "$\\int dy/(1-y) = -\\ln|1-y|$. Absolute values keep starts below $0$ and above $1$.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/partial-fractions/state-02.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/partial-fractions/state-03.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/partial-fractions/step-03.mp4",
      "duration": 1.9667,
      "frames": 59,
      "masterFrames": [
       175,
       234
      ],
      "bytes": 81484,
      "codec": "h264"
     }
    },
    {
     "index": 4,
     "title": "Solve for $y$",
     "relation": "solve",
     "relationLabel": "Solve",
     "tex": "\\frac{y}{1 - y} = K e^{t} \\;\\Rightarrow\\; y = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-t}/K}",
     "explanation": "Here $K = y(0)/(1 - y(0))$ may have either sign, and $1/K = d$. The constant solutions $y = 0$ and $y = 1$, lost by the division, are added back. The $z = 1/y$ route was shorter.",
     "initialFrame": "animations/partial-fractions/state-03.jpg",
     "finalFrame": "animations/partial-fractions/state-04.jpg",
     "transition": {
      "src": "animations/partial-fractions/step-04.mp4",
      "duration": 2.9,
      "frames": 87,
      "masterFrames": [
